+MUMPS 5.8.2: parallel local RHS scatter (hsolve P14).
+
+When one working process owns all N pivot rows (KEEP(89) and the fully
+summed RHS count both equal N), each front owns a disjoint contiguous range
+of RHSINTR. Distribute fronts across one OpenMP team, retaining the original
+row permutation and optional scaling, and avoid unused MPI buffer allocations.
+The metadata helper only reads IW/KEEP/PTRIST/STEP. No reductions, pivot
+choices or solve arithmetic change. The original path handles other layouts,
+small matrices (N < 32768), and trees with fewer than 64 fronts.
+Applies to all four arithmetics; no new KEEP entries or application settings.
+
+Apply after the L0-blocking and pivot-extrema patches with build_mumps.sh.
+Validation and timings: results/p14_measurements.md and p14_scatter_probe.cpp.
+This is an hsolve modification of MUMPS, distributed under CeCILL-C.
+
